Short:        PC Engine/TurboGrafx-16 emulator
Author:       Juan Antonio Gomez Galvez (GUS Entertainment), z00p
Uploader:     Zoopster (JCEC_1@yahoo.co.uk)
Type:         misc/emu
Version:      @VERSION@
Replaces:     misc/emu/AmiPCEngine.lha
Architecture: m68k-amigaos
Requires:     AGA, a fast CPU (PiStorm, fast 68060 or similar)
Distribution: Aminet
Kurz:         PC-Engine/TurboGrafx-16-Emulator

AmiPCEngine is a PC Engine / TurboGrafx-16 emulator for AGA Amigas, by
Juan Antonio Gomez Galvez and z00p, in 68020+ assembly. It plays HuCard games
(.pce files). It takes over the machine while a game runs and drives
the Amiga's custom chips directly, or a Picasso96 (RTG) screen.

History
-------
Juan began AmiPC-Engine about 1997; a first version was "abandoned due
the Amiga AGA limitations". Version 0.1 followed in 2011, and the
preview 0.3 on Aminet on 30 June 2020 (misc/emu/amipc-engine.lha, 4 of
6 sound channels, one sprite palette). His later version 0.5 (June
2021) was never released. In 2026 Juan sent his sources. This community
update, released with his permission, is built from them and finishes
what he started: all 6 sound channels with DDA samples, every sprite palette
on an RTG screen, and full speed on an A1200 with a PiStorm. His
v0.3 stays on Aminet as it is.

New in 2.0
----------
AGA now shows the PC Engine's own colours and every sprite palette.
Two programs: AGA and RTG (the menu opens on the RTG screen, no 15 kHz
screen needed). A fast machine is needed: a PiStorm, a fast 68060 or
similar; 68030 and 68020 machines are no longer supported. A new
launcher: Screen and Scanlines in the window, a pad type for each
port, the backup RAM state. Blazing Lazers' drums no longer click.
The Debug versions are available on request. See CHANGES.txt.

New in 1.4
----------
Controls answer a frame sooner: each emulated frame starts at the PC
Engine's vertical blank, so a press shows on screen 20 ms earlier. On RTG
the pad is read again just before a late frame start, a further 11 to 14
ms on an A1200 with a PiStorm. Parodius Da! no longer slows down on AGA
after a screen flash. See CHANGES.txt.

New in 1.3
----------
More games run or look right: TaleSpin, Cyber Cross, Lode Runner: Lost
Labyrinth, Momotarou Densetsu Gaiden and II, Power Tennis, Bikkuriman
World, Benkei Gaiden and Dragon Egg!. Sprites keep in step with a
scrolling background, and sounds change speaker less often. See
CHANGES.txt.

New in 1.2
----------
Backup RAM saves: games that save (high scores, progress) keep them in a
Saves drawer, one file per game. More games run or look right, from a
test of the whole HuCard library against Mesen: Order of the Griffon,
Coryoon, Cyber Core, Download, Battle Royale, Night Creatures, Energy,
World Circuit, Fighting Run and others. See CHANGES.txt.

Requirements
------------
- An AGA Amiga with AmigaOS 3.0 or later and a fast CPU: an A1200
  with a PiStorm, a fast 68060 or similar. Tested on a PiStorm A1200.
- RTG icon: Picasso96 and a 16-bit screen mode. Without them it falls
  back to the AGA screen.

Installation
------------
Unpack the archive anywhere. In the AmiPCEngine drawer start AGA
(AGA video output) or RTG (Picasso96 screen, ToolType RTG). Choose
Insert, pick a .pce file in the Homebrew drawer or anywhere else, then
Power ON. Esc returns to the menu. See ReadMe.txt in the drawer for
the keys and pads (keyboard, Amiga joystick, CD32 pad).

No games are included. You need HuCard images of your own, copies you
may legally have.

Limits
------
Not all games work. Not supported: CD-ROM games, SuperGrafx.
Sound: 6 PSG channels on the Amiga's 4, the
loudest four at each frame. Tested by us on an A1200 with a PiStorm
(RTG and AGA) and in WinUAE. Not tested on a real 68060 card or ECS.
The full list is in ReadMe.txt.

